<title>USA: Duff &amp; Phelps puts Duke on rating watch.</title>
<headline>Duff &amp; Phelps puts Duke on rating watch.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Duff &amp; Phelps Credit Rating Co said Monday it placed the rating of Duke Power Co on watch for a possible downgrade and PanEnergy Corp on watch for a possible upgrade after the two companies announced a merger agreement.</p>
<p>The ratings agency said the stock-swap merger, valued at about $7.7 billion, could potentially weaken Duke Power's rating since it is merging with what Duff &amp; Phelps called a &quot;financially weaker entity.&quot;</p>
<p>Duke Power is an electrical utility that serves 1.8-million customers in North Carolina and South Carolina. PanEnergy is the parent of two natural gas transportation and storage companies.</p>
<p>- Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787</p>
</text>
